+ * @sm: Pointer to EAP state machine allocated with eap_peer_sm_init()
+ * Returns: 1 if EAP state was changed or 0 if not
+ *
+ * This function advances EAP state machine to a new state to match with t=
he
+ * current variables. This should be called whenever variables used by the=
